-------------------

vidyut (vidyut-prakriya, vidyut-kosha, vidyut-sandhi, vidyut-lipi,
vidyut-chandas, vidyut-cheda) is by the Ambuda project,
https://github.com/ambuda-org/vidyut, and is licensed under the MIT License.
It is used as a library. Its linguistic data is downloaded at run time and is
not redistributed in this repository.

The Digital Corpus of Sanskrit (DCS) is by Oliver Hellwig,
https://github.com/OliverHellwig/sanskrit, and is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
Citation: Hellwig, Oliver (2010-2024): The Digital Corpus of Sanskrit (DCS).
The file mayur/gold/ramayana_bala_1.json is an excerpt converted from the DCS
CoNLL-U files (Ramayana, Balakanda 1), transliterated to SLP1. Frequency tables
and the gloss dictionary derived from DCS are built locally by script and are
not committed to this repository.

The Monier-Williams Sanskrit-English Dictionary is provided by the Cologne
Digital Sanskrit Dictionaries, https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de. Its
licence is unclear. It may optionally be fetched by script for local use only.
It is never committed or redistributed in this repository.

No glosses or translations were copied from valmiki.iitk.ac.in or
valmikiramayan.net.
